--TEST--
A class or an interface in a class body is one `E0233` where it is written, while an enum there is accepted — `rule:enums/class-scoped-enum`, `rule:classes/a-type-is-declared-at-file-scope`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// `rule:enums/class-scoped-enum`: an enum is a closed list of integers. A
// class or an interface has members, layout and dispatch of its own, so it is
// declared at file scope.
final class Order {
    enum Status { Open, Paid }

    final class Line {}

    interface Priced {}
}

echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0233]: a class or an interface is not declared in a class body
  --> case.nvs:8:5
%A
error[E0233]: a class or an interface is not declared in a class body
   --> case.nvs:10:5
%A
error: aborting due to 2 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
